# Design system sync

When you change **visual UI** (layout, copy, colours, typography, spacing, interaction states, or new screens), update the design system in the **same change** unless the user explicitly says to skip it.

## PalaLive product (prefer this)

Hub: `/design-system/palalive` — foundations, components, screens only for venue TV + staff.

| Production surface | Shared component(s) | Design-system preview |
|--------------------|---------------------|------------------------|
| `/screen/[screenSlug]` Idle | `PalaLiveIdle` | `/design-system/preview/palalive?state=idle` |
| `/screen/…` Social Night | `PalaLiveSocialView` / `PalaLiveModeWaiting` | `…?state=social-waiting\|social-pregame\|social-ingame\|social-postgame` |
| `/screen/…` Showcase | `PalaLiveShowcaseView` / `PalaLiveModeWaiting` / `PalaLiveShowcaseEndgameView` | `…?state=showcase-waiting\|showcase\|showcase-endgame` |
| `/staff/…/showcase` | `ControlPanel` `variant=palalive-staff` | `/design-system/preview/control?state=&variant=palalive-staff` |
| Social staff `/matchplay/*` | matchplay pages + `StaffAppFrame` | `/design-system/preview/matchplay?state=` |

**Catalog tabs:** `app/design-system/palalive/lib/screen-catalog.ts` — add new TV/staff states there; they appear on `/design-system/palalive/screens`.

**Tokens:** `app/styles/palalive-tokens.css` — foundations page swatches; staff + TV shells share this file.

## v4 legacy (player / court / old spectator)

| Production surface | Shared component(s) | Design-system preview |
|--------------------|---------------------|------------------------|
| `/control` | `ControlPanel`, `MatchConfirmation` | `/design-system/preview/control?state=` (no palalive-staff) |
| `/setup`, `/playing` | `SetupDisplay`, `PlayingDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/setup?state=`, `/playing?state=` |
| Court TV | `CourtDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/court?state=` |
| Spectator TV (legacy) | `SpectatorDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/spectator?state=` |
| `/session-review` | `SessionReviewDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/session-review` |
| `/game/[id]` | `GameDetailDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/game` |

## How to stay in sync

1. **Prefer shared display components** — previews render the same component as production with mock data / `preview` props.
2. **New PalaLive screen state** — extend `screen-catalog.ts` and the relevant preview page (`preview/palalive` or `preview/control` / `matchplay`).
3. **CSS / tokens** — PalaLive visual changes → check `/design-system/palalive/foundations` and `/components`; v4 token changes → `/design-system/tokens` etc.
4. **Staff footer / mobile chrome** — CTAs use `.palalive-staff-footer` pinned in the phone column; keep Confirm / Setup / End aligned.
5. **Mock data** — `lib/palalive/mock-*.ts` and `app/design-system/lib/*` stay aligned with preview states.

## Before finishing

- [ ] Identified which PalaLive (or v4) preview route(s) mirror the changed UI
- [ ] Updated `screen-catalog.ts` / preview config / hub if needed
- [ ] Did not leave production-only markup that previews no longer exercise
